# Tests

Extends the core rule and `AGENTS.md`.

- Test behavior, not implementation details. Cover success, validation, error, and edge
  cases. Mock external services only.
- Never weaken, skip, or delete tests to make checks pass, and don't change production code
  only to suit a broken test.
- Web: Vitest + Testing Library + jsdom, co-located `*.test.ts(x)`. Query by role and
  accessible name. Mock `next/navigation` with `vi.mock` and network with
  `vi.stubGlobal("fetch", …)`.
- API: Pytest in `apps/api/tests/`. Use the `client` fixture (`conftest.py`), which builds an
  isolated app with `create_app(Settings(...))`. Warnings are errors.
- `tests/test_openapi.py` guards the shared contract. If it fails, run
  `pnpm contracts:generate`.
- No E2E framework yet. Don't add one unless asked.
- Narrowest first: `pnpm --filter @orbit/web exec vitest run <file>`,
  `cd apps/api && uv run pytest <file>`. Then `pnpm check`.
